WEBVTT

00:00:20.180 --> 00:00:23.810
<i>This is the sun, this is the moon.</i>

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:27.270
<i>This mountain is really the earth.</i>

00:00:30.780 --> 00:00:33.900
<i>And this is grandma.</i>

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:57.890
My, how splendid.

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:00.970
Hello, Mrs. Yamada.

00:01:01.560 --> 00:01:05.310
I've never seen such a magnificent...

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:08.400
Yup, they're my little babies.

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:09.980
What species?

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:12.900
This is a Mino Chrysanthemum,
this is...

00:01:12.980 --> 00:01:15.110
No, I mean the caterpillar.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:20.530
No idea.

00:01:21.370 --> 00:01:25.250
Grow into a butterfly
just as gaudy as that flower.

00:01:28.830 --> 00:01:30.710
Mother!

00:01:31.750 --> 00:01:34.170
<i>That's our grandma.</i>

00:01:44.180 --> 00:01:48.140
<i>And my mother and me, Nonoko.</i>

00:01:49.230 --> 00:01:52.270
What am I going to make
for dinner tonight?

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.320
I know, I'll go for it!
Something really special!

00:01:59.410 --> 00:02:00.700
What are we having?

00:02:01.030 --> 00:02:03.620
We had curry last week,
curry two days ago,

00:02:03.700 --> 00:02:06.000
tonight... curry!

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.160
What?

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:22.050
<i>And this is my father</i>
<i>and my older brother.</i>

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.640
What's the use
of all this studying, Dad?

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.140
Listen, Noboru,

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:33.110
studying is not about
what's useful or not.

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:36.820
The studying that seems useless
may turn out to be useful.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:39.200
On the other hand, it might be that.

00:02:39.780 --> 00:02:43.070
studying that doesn't seem
not useful may not be,

00:02:43.660 --> 00:02:46.870
but then, studying that seems useless
may then be useful.

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.830
But when you really need it,
it's not about useful or useless.

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:54.170
What are you going on about?

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.510
So I still have to study.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:31.460
I get it.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:36.170
If my father had been smart
and really cool

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.050
and my mother had been gorgeous
and a great cook

00:03:40.970 --> 00:03:46.220
and our family had been rich,
my whole life would've been different.

00:03:49.930 --> 00:03:52.440
If only one of them...

00:03:52.520 --> 00:03:54.770
Don't be ridiculous.

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:59.360
If we hadn't married,
there'd be no you and no Nonoko.

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:02.400
Without the two of us,
you wouldn't be here.

00:04:03.280 --> 00:04:04.910
No, that's wrong.

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:09.580
If I had cooler parents,
I'd just be their kid instead.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:11.080
How stupid.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:14.960
Don't you know about
stamens and pistils?

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:16.080
You tell him.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:17.920
You can't choose your parents.

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.550
No, I can't accept that.
Something's not right.

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:26.760
Because I'm me, Dad's Dad
and Mom's Mom.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:29.970
What is that supposed to mean?

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:33.140
Who am I?

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.190
Where did I come from?

00:04:37.310 --> 00:04:38.730
Where am I?

00:04:39.940 --> 00:04:41.230
Who am I?

00:04:42.900 --> 00:04:44.450
I get it.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:49.370
So, there was a time
when Dad and Mom weren't married.

00:05:13.520 --> 00:05:18.230
<i>Takashi and Matsuko are off</i>
<i>to a great start in their new life.</i>

00:05:18.310 --> 00:05:21.020
<i>Let's give them a warm send-off.</i>

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:27.070
<i>Congratulations, Takashi and Matsuko.</i>

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:33.410
<i>I also offer warm wishes</i>
<i>to their parents and relatives.</i>

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:44.340
<i>Now, your prospects are boundless,</i>

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:49.390
<i>and you're embarking for the wide</i>
<i>open world under billowing sails.</i>

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:06.490
<i>Life, as they say, has its ups and downs.</i>

00:06:06.570 --> 00:06:11.780
<i>At times, the waves may taunt you,</i>
<i>tossing you in their swells.</i>

00:06:12.240 --> 00:06:14.540
<i>But take heart.</i>

00:06:14.620 --> 00:06:18.790
<i>It's hard to stick with it</i>
<i>and make it on your own,</i>

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:24.960
<i>but even a couple of losers can survive</i>
<i>most things if they're together.</i>

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:34.100
<i>So listen, take my advice,</i>
<i>and have children as soon as you can.</i>

00:06:35.140 --> 00:06:40.770
<i>Children are the best reason</i>
<i>for riding out life's storms.</i>

00:07:50.380 --> 00:07:55.300
<i>Nowadays people say child-rearing</i>
<i>is challenging and difficult,</i>

00:07:55.390 --> 00:07:58.100
<i>but we've done it from time immemorial.</i>

00:07:58.720 --> 00:08:01.390
<i>Children grow even without parents.</i>

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:05.100
<i>So hold them close to your heart</i>
<i>as they crawl, then walk.</i>

00:08:05.190 --> 00:08:08.400
<i>They'll be fine.</i>

00:08:19.290 --> 00:08:22.460
<i>Children make you</i>
<i>appreciate your own parents.</i>

00:08:23.210 --> 00:08:26.330
<i>Parents may seem to do nothing</i>
<i>but order you around,</i>

00:08:26.420 --> 00:08:30.670
<i>but they'll baby-sit your kids</i>
<i>and sometimes give them toys.</i>

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:33.550
<i>Nowadays young people</i>

00:08:33.630 --> 00:08:38.970
<i>turn that saying about appreciating</i>
<i>parents to their own advantage.</i>

00:08:39.720 --> 00:08:42.680
<i>But I guess that's part of it too.</i>

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:48.610
<i>If things work out,</i>
<i>you even get the real estate.</i>

00:08:51.440 --> 00:08:54.150
<i>So, Matsuko and Takashi,</i>

00:08:54.490 --> 00:08:57.200
<i>start looking after your folks!</i>

00:08:57.700 --> 00:09:00.910
I hope you know the land is in my name.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:04.410
Excuse me, Mother, but I built this house.

00:09:04.500 --> 00:09:06.920
Without land, there's no house.

00:09:07.000 --> 00:09:10.040
And we are grateful to you,

00:09:10.130 --> 00:09:12.550
but I've worked hard, too.

00:09:12.630 --> 00:09:15.300
Your room gets the best light.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:16.880
Thanks for nothing.

00:09:17.260 --> 00:09:21.310
Of course, it does. It's on my land.

00:09:21.390 --> 00:09:25.520
Besides, why do you always insist
you built it by yourself?

00:09:25.600 --> 00:09:28.980
I hate to contradict you,
but I definitely built...

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:31.230
That's enough!

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:32.610
Both of you.

00:09:32.690 --> 00:09:36.610
That's right! What's the point
of all this bickering?

00:09:36.700 --> 00:09:38.110
Listen to Noboru.

00:09:38.450 --> 00:09:40.240
In the end, it'll all be mine.

00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:09.770
<i>And what should you fear most</i>
<i>on this lifelong voyage?</i>

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:12.480
<i>Wild storms and rip tides?</i>

00:10:20.530 --> 00:10:25.040
<i>No. Beware the calm waters</i>
<i>when there's hardly a ripple in sight.</i>

00:10:25.540 --> 00:10:29.750
<i>As long as a family holds</i>
<i>each other tight, they can somehow</i>

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:32.380
<i>weather the wildest seas.</i>

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:34.630
<i>But calm waters are another story.</i>

00:10:34.710 --> 00:10:38.880
<i>The wind dies down,</i>
<i>you sigh and relax,</i>

00:10:38.970 --> 00:10:41.220
<i>loosening your hold.</i>

00:10:41.930 --> 00:10:44.470
<i>But take care, Matsuko and Takashi!</i>

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:49.390
<i>If you selfishly please only yourselves,</i>

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:52.310
<i>you may lose each other.</i>

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:00.910
<i>You'll never see the sharks</i>
<i>gathering around you.</i>

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:09.410
<i>And how will you guide your ship?</i>

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:14.170
Without a wind or even a course?

00:11:14.250 --> 00:11:17.510
If you row blindly, right, no, left...

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:22.550
<i>No, right after all, you'll never agree.</i>

00:11:22.890 --> 00:11:26.600
<i>You may even wonder why</i>
<i>you're stuck on the same boat at all.</i>

00:11:28.310 --> 00:11:30.640
<i>Your family's about to fall apart.</i>

00:11:31.600 --> 00:11:32.730
Turn right there!

00:11:32.810 --> 00:11:33.770
Are you sure?

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:34.980
Turn left!

00:11:35.060 --> 00:11:37.190
Right, right! No, left, left!

00:11:37.270 --> 00:11:38.360
Which way?

00:11:38.440 --> 00:11:39.940
Oh dear, maybe right.

00:11:40.030 --> 00:11:41.570
Which is it?

00:11:50.370 --> 00:11:52.290
We came so close.

00:11:52.370 --> 00:11:53.670
Our turn!

00:11:53.750 --> 00:11:55.670
A FAMILY CRISIS

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:05.390
We're taking the long way around.

00:12:05.470 --> 00:12:07.010
You should've turned!

00:12:07.100 --> 00:12:08.510
No, no, go straight!

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.890
No, it's that way. Are you crazy?

00:12:10.980 --> 00:12:12.440
It's this way, Dad!

00:12:12.940 --> 00:12:15.020
Quiet! All of you.

00:12:16.150 --> 00:12:18.440
Nonoko's the only one who's quiet.

00:12:19.150 --> 00:12:21.570
Wait a minute... She's not here.

00:12:23.700 --> 00:12:24.820
What?

00:12:25.320 --> 00:12:26.740
Where is she?

00:12:26.820 --> 00:12:28.580
Stop the car.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:35.580
Where did we lose her?

00:12:36.040 --> 00:12:39.090
Noboru, weren't you with her?

00:12:39.670 --> 00:12:42.720
Yeah, while Dad and I
were waiting for you.

00:12:43.300 --> 00:12:46.010
Maybe she got bored and wandered off.

00:12:46.090 --> 00:12:48.390
No, I remember her on the bench.

00:12:54.770 --> 00:12:56.690
I'm so sorry.

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.690
What took you so long?

00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:03.570
Sorry, I didn't mean to.

00:13:03.650 --> 00:13:05.950
I could have done some shopping, too.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.910
I wanted to look at baseball bats.

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:16.500
<i>I'm sure she's still there.</i>

00:13:23.590 --> 00:13:27.260
It's all because you kept yelling about
how late we were.

00:13:27.340 --> 00:13:30.600
Don't blame me.
You're the ones who were late.

00:13:30.680 --> 00:13:36.100
You all got so excited,
you just left poor Nonoko behind.

00:13:36.190 --> 00:13:39.480
Like you weren't there yourself, Grandma.

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:42.730
We were looking for
your flannel underwear!

00:13:42.820 --> 00:13:45.820
The store will close. I'll never make it.

00:13:45.900 --> 00:13:48.320
Stop thinking about yourself.

00:13:48.410 --> 00:13:51.490
What if something terrible
happens to Nonoko?

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.580
Something terrible?

00:13:54.750 --> 00:13:56.830
You don't mean... kidnapped?

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.840
She's so adorable, just like me.

00:14:04.340 --> 00:14:06.130
This is no time for jokes!

00:14:07.050 --> 00:14:10.590
I hope she doesn't forget.

00:14:10.680 --> 00:14:11.970
Forget what?

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:13.600
The PTA mantra.

00:14:14.640 --> 00:14:17.980
"Don't talk to strangers."

00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:21.310
That's what you teach children?

00:14:21.400 --> 00:14:24.860
It's like saying
all strangers are thieves.

00:14:24.940 --> 00:14:27.360
Nonoko's fine. Those teeth!

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:31.410
Hey, cake! Gimme some!

00:14:31.910 --> 00:14:33.660
Just one bite.

00:14:33.740 --> 00:14:34.620
OK!

00:14:36.870 --> 00:14:38.290
One chomp of those teeth!

00:14:38.370 --> 00:14:39.500
Enough!

00:14:44.090 --> 00:14:47.630
Please, our daughter
is about to be kidnapped!

00:14:51.640 --> 00:14:53.050
We can't even call.

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:55.760
We should've called before.

00:14:55.850 --> 00:14:57.470
I told you to buy a cellphone.

00:14:57.560 --> 00:14:59.310
You keep quiet!

00:15:01.150 --> 00:15:04.150
Oh, Nonoko!

00:15:30.840 --> 00:15:32.220
Are you lost?

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:37.060
Huh? So, you're waiting for someone?

00:15:45.150 --> 00:15:46.690
Who are you waiting for?

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.240
Can't you talk?

00:15:51.150 --> 00:15:53.410
Then why don't you say anything?

00:15:53.820 --> 00:15:59.040
I'm... I'm not supposed to talk to...

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:05.080
I know, "Don't talk to strangers," right?

00:16:06.880 --> 00:16:12.630
You're very grown-up because
you're careful. You can talk now.

00:16:13.220 --> 00:16:15.050
You should hear my story.

00:16:15.550 --> 00:16:20.220
My father and mother
and grandma and brother all got lost.

00:16:20.720 --> 00:16:22.350
Did you lose someone?

00:16:24.310 --> 00:16:25.350
My mommy.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:26.980
Your mommy?

00:16:27.400 --> 00:16:31.240
My mommy went away.

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:35.740
I know. There've been
a lot of missing parents lately.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:39.620
But it's only your mom, you'll find her.

00:16:45.370 --> 00:16:48.670
Excuse me, this is Toshio Kimura.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:50.630
Can you please call his mom?

00:16:51.300 --> 00:16:52.130
Oh, he's lost?

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:54.430
No, he's not, they were separated.

00:16:55.430 --> 00:16:56.680
Right.

00:16:58.260 --> 00:17:01.020
And your first name, Mr. Kimura?

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:02.270
-Toshio.
-Toshio.

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:03.980
Toshio, then.

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:07.150
Wait here a minute, OK?

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:12.280
And you? Are you his sister?

00:17:12.860 --> 00:17:14.360
No, no relation.

00:17:14.450 --> 00:17:17.280
My whole family's lost.

00:17:30.880 --> 00:17:36.510
<i>Poor little, poor little lost pussy cat</i>

00:17:44.730 --> 00:17:46.560
Stop crying, we're here.

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:17.630
What? She went with her mother?

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:19.840
I'm her mother!

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:21.600
Oh, is that so?

00:18:21.680 --> 00:18:24.560
How dare you give her to a stranger!

00:18:25.140 --> 00:18:28.310
Maybe it wasn't her mother,
but it was no stranger.

00:18:28.890 --> 00:18:31.110
No stranger? Who could it be?

00:18:31.190 --> 00:18:32.690
I don't know anyone...

00:18:34.690 --> 00:18:37.070
Someone pretending to be friendly.

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:41.410
No, she recognized Nonoko.

00:18:41.490 --> 00:18:42.530
That wasn't her mother!

00:18:42.620 --> 00:18:44.830
Calm down! And then?

00:18:46.410 --> 00:18:47.960
I'm terribly sorry.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:51.250
Nonoko went off happily with someone

00:18:51.330 --> 00:18:54.090
who seemed like her mother.

00:18:55.050 --> 00:18:57.550
Oh no! Who can it be?

00:18:58.050 --> 00:18:59.840
Will you please page Nonoko?

00:19:00.340 --> 00:19:03.680
Actually... they went out
that exit together.

00:19:03.760 --> 00:19:04.640
Not here.

00:19:04.720 --> 00:19:05.560
Come on!

00:19:11.100 --> 00:19:13.190
That's some family.

00:19:22.450 --> 00:19:25.120
Dad, where are you racing off to?

00:19:25.200 --> 00:19:27.040
-I'm chasing it!
-What?

00:19:27.450 --> 00:19:29.540
The car Nonoko's in!

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:30.910
What kind of car?

00:19:36.960 --> 00:19:40.260
We don't even know which way it went!

00:19:41.220 --> 00:19:44.430
She'll be fine.
Nonoko knew the lady, right?

00:19:44.510 --> 00:19:46.430
I bet she took her home.

00:19:47.100 --> 00:19:49.350
I'm sure Noboru's right.

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:53.230
Sure, that must be it.

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:56.400
Don't be so sure.
You can't trust anyone these days.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:57.650
Mother!

00:19:57.980 --> 00:20:01.150
Don't you think
you should notify the police?

00:20:01.530 --> 00:20:02.530
The police!

00:20:02.610 --> 00:20:04.160
How would we explain?

00:20:04.740 --> 00:20:06.620
Make a full confession.

00:20:07.080 --> 00:20:07.950
Confession?

00:20:08.040 --> 00:20:12.960
That four grown people neglected
and abandoned a young girl.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:16.380
Say, does Nonoko have a key?

00:20:17.920 --> 00:20:18.920
Let's go home!

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:52.160
Nonoko!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:56.960
Nonoko!

00:20:57.380 --> 00:20:58.340
Nonoko!

00:20:58.960 --> 00:21:00.960
POCHI

00:21:02.130 --> 00:21:02.970
Nonoko!

00:21:07.050 --> 00:21:08.260
Not here.

00:21:08.350 --> 00:21:10.680
Of course not, it was locked.

00:21:14.850 --> 00:21:17.060
Hello.

00:21:19.060 --> 00:21:21.570
Oh, thank goodness!

00:21:21.650 --> 00:21:24.820
Thank you! Thank you so much!

00:21:26.200 --> 00:21:30.240
Thank you!
We were looking everywhere for her.

00:21:30.330 --> 00:21:32.410
I'm so sorry for all this.

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:38.250
Yes, we'll be right over.

00:21:39.080 --> 00:21:41.590
You even made her dinner!

00:21:42.420 --> 00:21:47.840
You're so very kind.
How can we possibly thank you?

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.060
They finally got home.

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:58.770
They're coming right over.

00:21:58.850 --> 00:22:00.190
I'm sorry, auntie.

00:22:00.900 --> 00:22:02.820
Oh, it's nothing.

00:22:02.900 --> 00:22:07.570
I can't wait to hear
their side of the story.

00:22:19.830 --> 00:22:22.880
<i>Joyful laughter breaks the silence</i>
<i>of an autumn eve.</i>

00:22:22.960 --> 00:22:24.250
<i>Basho.</i>

00:22:26.550 --> 00:22:30.890
<i>Look up and see the blue skies</i>

00:22:31.140 --> 00:22:35.060
<i>The white clouds</i>

00:22:35.310 --> 00:22:40.900
<i>One of these days</i>
<i>It'll all work out</i>

00:23:03.380 --> 00:23:06.000
<i>Next stop, Luncheon Court.</i>

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:13.720
<i>Stopping.</i>

00:23:16.770 --> 00:23:19.390
What did you call this stop?

00:23:20.020 --> 00:23:22.100
Can you stand back, ma'am?

00:23:26.190 --> 00:23:28.110
HOME ECONOMICS WIZARD

00:23:28.740 --> 00:23:31.110
Oh, dear, it started raining.

00:23:37.950 --> 00:23:39.500
The laundry!

00:23:44.880 --> 00:23:45.920
Huh?

00:23:52.220 --> 00:23:53.510
What's the fuss?

00:23:59.140 --> 00:24:01.430
That's right! I'd already brought it in.

00:24:01.520 --> 00:24:03.520
You never even hung it up!

00:24:05.230 --> 00:24:08.440
I'm going out. Can I get you anything?

00:24:08.820 --> 00:24:11.150
Oh! There was something.

00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:16.240
What was it? Uhm... Uhm...

00:24:17.950 --> 00:24:20.080
OK, then, I'm going.

00:24:22.910 --> 00:24:26.420
It's just that... Oh, what was it?

00:24:38.050 --> 00:24:39.640
Wait, wait, wait, wait...

00:24:39.720 --> 00:24:41.430
What is it?

00:24:44.810 --> 00:24:47.270
Uhm... That is... Uhm...

00:24:47.770 --> 00:24:49.900
Why don't you just give up?

00:24:51.900 --> 00:24:53.400
Oh! Bread!

00:24:57.200 --> 00:24:59.120
Get it yourself!

00:24:59.910 --> 00:25:01.450
Mom!

00:25:03.000 --> 00:25:04.460
Money, money.

00:25:06.000 --> 00:25:07.250
I'm home.

00:25:09.130 --> 00:25:11.500
I guess Mom's not here.

00:25:13.760 --> 00:25:14.930
Wow, noodles.

00:25:15.680 --> 00:25:17.300
And the water's boiling.

00:25:17.890 --> 00:25:20.810
Great, I'll go ahead and eat them.

00:25:27.230 --> 00:25:29.310
Oh, you're home.

00:25:39.570 --> 00:25:40.950
You were hiding!

00:25:46.210 --> 00:25:47.330
Hm?

00:25:48.960 --> 00:25:50.590
The bulb's out.

00:25:51.170 --> 00:25:53.550
That's no good. Better change it.

00:25:55.130 --> 00:25:58.300
Oh, darn... no spares.

00:25:58.390 --> 00:26:01.220
Switch it with one you're not using.

00:26:03.520 --> 00:26:04.850
Up we go.

00:26:08.440 --> 00:26:09.980
I'm just borrowing it.

00:26:10.060 --> 00:26:11.820
Ouch, it's hot.

00:26:15.900 --> 00:26:17.110
Tea.

00:26:17.200 --> 00:26:18.450
-Me, too.
-Me, too.

00:26:18.530 --> 00:26:19.780
Me, too.

00:26:19.860 --> 00:26:23.330
I'm busy washing the dishes.
Get in here, one of you!

00:26:26.370 --> 00:26:28.330
Rock paper scissors.

00:26:31.170 --> 00:26:33.670
Get your cup out.

00:26:39.630 --> 00:26:42.300
The dishes are all yours.

00:26:45.060 --> 00:26:47.230
Mr. Tanaka says he's coming over.

00:26:47.310 --> 00:26:49.480
What? Oh, no.

00:26:52.940 --> 00:26:54.690
Better tidy up a little.

00:27:00.320 --> 00:27:01.240
Ouch.

00:27:13.840 --> 00:27:15.460
Hey, what are you doing?

00:27:15.550 --> 00:27:17.550
I'll say we're spring cleaning!

00:27:24.760 --> 00:27:26.680
MARRIAGE YAMADA STYLE

00:27:30.770 --> 00:27:32.690
It's on the kitchen table.

00:27:34.980 --> 00:27:36.190
No, it's not.

00:27:36.900 --> 00:27:39.190
Are you sure? I know I left it.

00:27:39.280 --> 00:27:41.070
<i>It isn't here.</i>

00:27:41.570 --> 00:27:43.370
Where did you look?

00:27:43.450 --> 00:27:46.530
It's a manila envelope
that says OKK in red.

00:27:47.040 --> 00:27:48.540
Is this it, sir?

00:27:50.830 --> 00:27:53.040
Oh, uh... OK. Well...

00:27:54.880 --> 00:27:56.840
if it's gone, it's gone.

00:27:58.460 --> 00:28:00.470
-Hey.
-Here.

00:28:00.760 --> 00:28:02.970
That's 20 years of marriage for you.

00:28:03.550 --> 00:28:04.720
I meant the paper.

00:28:04.800 --> 00:28:06.430
When I'm done.

00:28:08.600 --> 00:28:09.600
Impressive.

00:28:09.680 --> 00:28:11.680
POCHI

00:28:18.110 --> 00:28:20.150
Can you pick up a few things?

00:28:20.240 --> 00:28:21.110
Sure.

00:28:21.360 --> 00:28:26.200
Lettuce, cucumber, ham,
light bulbs, and garbage bags.

00:28:26.570 --> 00:28:27.950
I'll make a list.

00:28:28.030 --> 00:28:29.040
No, I've got it.

00:28:33.540 --> 00:28:35.960
Lettuce, cucumber, ham...

00:28:36.790 --> 00:28:38.670
light bulbs, and garbage bags, right?

00:28:39.250 --> 00:28:40.170
I told you.

00:28:40.510 --> 00:28:43.050
All I forgot was to buy them.

00:28:45.590 --> 00:28:47.930
Lettuce, cucumber...

00:28:53.350 --> 00:28:55.690
Let's see...

00:28:57.770 --> 00:28:58.650
Make up your mind.

00:28:59.320 --> 00:29:01.400
Have you decided?

00:29:02.070 --> 00:29:03.740
Just hurry up.

00:29:07.370 --> 00:29:09.030
I'll take the Shanghai Special.

00:29:09.490 --> 00:29:10.620
Me too.

00:29:11.490 --> 00:29:12.870
Two Shanghai Specials.

00:29:19.040 --> 00:29:21.380
Oh, you're still here?

00:29:21.460 --> 00:29:22.800
What do you mean, "still"?

00:29:23.170 --> 00:29:25.630
Can't I rest on my day off?

00:29:26.130 --> 00:29:28.640
Usually, you're off at Pachinko.

00:29:29.390 --> 00:29:32.470
Nope, I'm giving it a rest.
How about some tea?

00:29:33.600 --> 00:29:35.850
And noodles for lunch.

00:29:35.940 --> 00:29:37.270
Yes, dear.

00:29:39.270 --> 00:29:42.150
Actually, make that coffee, not tea!

00:29:46.320 --> 00:29:49.370
And the bathroom's a wreck.

00:29:50.160 --> 00:29:51.280
Clean it up.

00:29:51.950 --> 00:29:55.000
And when you go shopping,
I need cigarettes.

00:29:55.620 --> 00:29:58.120
What a pain in the neck!

00:30:02.090 --> 00:30:04.510
Honey! Honey!

00:30:07.220 --> 00:30:08.680
Where's your mother?

00:30:09.140 --> 00:30:10.470
Out playing Pachinko.

00:30:12.430 --> 00:30:16.270
<i>...only one sacrifice fly</i>
<i>in the fifth inning.</i>

00:30:16.350 --> 00:30:18.730
<i>Kuwata has pitched.</i>

00:30:18.810 --> 00:30:23.610
<i>And he hits it. Right where he wants it.</i>
<i>But he's there to catch it.</i>

00:30:23.690 --> 00:30:26.990
<i>And he catches it with ease.</i>
<i>That's the third out.</i>

00:30:27.070 --> 00:30:28.360
<i>The Giants will move to</i>

00:30:28.450 --> 00:30:29.910
<i>the offense in the bottom</i>

00:30:29.990 --> 00:30:33.030
<i>of the eighth inning with one out.</i>

00:30:33.120 --> 00:30:36.040
<i>Tonight's program will be extended...</i>

00:30:36.120 --> 00:30:38.710
My program's about to start.

00:30:38.790 --> 00:30:40.920
<i>In the top of the eighth inning,</i>

00:30:41.000 --> 00:30:43.250
<i>Kuwata really showed his skills.</i>

00:30:43.340 --> 00:30:46.210
<i>As a pitcher,</i>
<i>he is a brilliant defense player.</i>

00:30:46.300 --> 00:30:48.930
<i>He really is.</i>

00:30:49.010 --> 00:30:50.050
It's not over.

00:30:50.130 --> 00:30:52.800
But I was looking forward to it.

00:30:52.890 --> 00:30:53.890
No.

00:30:53.970 --> 00:30:55.430
It's a movie!

00:31:28.420 --> 00:31:30.760
Now nobody can watch.

00:31:30.840 --> 00:31:32.890
This is much more fun.

00:31:48.820 --> 00:31:50.320
I win!

00:32:47.710 --> 00:32:48.670
Hey, Noboru.

00:32:49.960 --> 00:32:50.920
Wanna play catch?

00:32:52.510 --> 00:32:53.630
Yeah.

00:32:53.720 --> 00:32:54.550
MALE BONDING

00:32:54.630 --> 00:32:56.050
NO TRESPASSING

00:33:01.100 --> 00:33:04.560
Wait, the dad's supposed to be
the catcher.

00:33:05.230 --> 00:33:06.440
Give me a break.

00:33:09.480 --> 00:33:13.400
OK, this signal is for a curveball,
this is for a fastball,

00:33:13.820 --> 00:33:15.320
and this is for a slider.

00:33:15.820 --> 00:33:17.660
Give me a break.

00:33:17.990 --> 00:33:20.870
Two outs, bases loaded,
you're the relief pitcher.

00:33:20.950 --> 00:33:23.750
I'm the starting pitcher type.

00:33:23.830 --> 00:33:25.160
Give me a break!

00:33:25.670 --> 00:33:27.250
Are you nuts?

00:33:27.330 --> 00:33:29.880
The team never even lets you pitch.

00:33:29.960 --> 00:33:32.550
That's why I want to start now.

00:33:33.970 --> 00:33:36.930
I see. OK, let's see
this starting pitcher pitch.

00:33:38.260 --> 00:33:41.060
It's still two outs, bases loaded.

00:33:41.140 --> 00:33:42.180
What?

00:33:58.990 --> 00:33:59.910
OK, pitch.

00:34:05.580 --> 00:34:07.000
Goddammit!

00:34:11.090 --> 00:34:12.880
What are you listening to?

00:34:15.170 --> 00:34:18.590
Listening over and over
will improve my English.

00:34:22.560 --> 00:34:24.180
It's not that easy.

00:34:24.600 --> 00:34:26.180
In my experience...

00:34:26.270 --> 00:34:28.270
Study!

00:34:28.350 --> 00:34:29.190
Study!

00:34:29.270 --> 00:34:32.730
Study!

00:34:53.590 --> 00:34:55.510
Repetition just doesn't work.

00:34:55.590 --> 00:34:56.800
I'm not you.

00:35:02.930 --> 00:35:05.060
How about a drop of sake?

00:35:05.140 --> 00:35:07.100
-Sure.
-But, dear...

00:35:15.610 --> 00:35:16.820
Pretty awful, huh?

00:35:19.740 --> 00:35:20.740
A little dry.

00:35:22.240 --> 00:35:23.990
-What did you say?
-Have you been...?

00:35:28.750 --> 00:35:29.660
Noboru!

00:35:29.750 --> 00:35:30.920
Noboru!

00:35:40.260 --> 00:35:42.930
Hey, Noboru, let's play catch.

00:35:44.800 --> 00:35:45.810
Why?

00:35:47.010 --> 00:35:51.100
Why? It's a form of parent-child bonding.

00:35:52.480 --> 00:35:54.440
Then it doesn't have to be catch.

00:35:55.060 --> 00:35:57.230
I get your point, but...

00:35:58.530 --> 00:36:01.610
We need the right setting.

00:36:02.660 --> 00:36:04.410
Forget it. Can't be bothered.

00:36:19.590 --> 00:36:22.550
Kids these days.

00:36:28.810 --> 00:36:31.100
A serious generation gap.

00:36:35.270 --> 00:36:37.190
PATERNAL SUPREMACY RESTORED

00:36:40.900 --> 00:36:43.070
Don't mix your rice into the soup!

00:36:43.150 --> 00:36:44.700
It's bad manners.

00:36:45.570 --> 00:36:47.370
Pour the soup over the rice.

00:36:50.330 --> 00:36:51.950
Excuse me, Father...

00:36:53.540 --> 00:36:54.710
What? Got a problem with that?

00:36:55.710 --> 00:36:57.210
Oh, suit yourself!

00:37:03.090 --> 00:37:05.800
See? Cement, then water.

00:37:06.510 --> 00:37:08.300
Uhm...

00:37:10.100 --> 00:37:11.390
Hmm...

00:37:11.470 --> 00:37:13.810
Quit dawdling. Make a choice.

00:37:15.020 --> 00:37:17.360
Use your chopsticks with purpose.

00:37:19.190 --> 00:37:20.980
That's my plate.

00:37:21.280 --> 00:37:22.610
Excuse me.

00:37:23.530 --> 00:37:25.910
You bit it, it's yours.

00:37:31.580 --> 00:37:34.290
Help me think of
an independent study topic.

00:37:34.910 --> 00:37:36.080
Think for yourself.

00:37:36.500 --> 00:37:38.710
It's "independent study," right?

00:37:39.380 --> 00:37:42.460
I know, but I'm coming up blank.

00:37:43.800 --> 00:37:46.010
You're free to do anything?

00:37:46.090 --> 00:37:47.590
Right, free.

00:37:47.680 --> 00:37:48.800
But...

00:37:49.760 --> 00:37:54.680
Total freedom makes it tough, doesn't it?

00:37:54.770 --> 00:37:56.390
Exactly.

00:37:58.440 --> 00:37:59.730
Complete freedom...

00:38:10.120 --> 00:38:13.040
Absolute freedom of choice...

00:38:18.960 --> 00:38:23.300
Glorious freedom...
The freedom of dreams...

00:38:23.710 --> 00:38:26.630
But when it comes on a silver platter...

00:38:31.680 --> 00:38:33.510
I haven't got a clue.

00:38:39.480 --> 00:38:41.270
Now he's a philosopher.

00:38:41.980 --> 00:38:44.860
He's probably worrying about
his retirement.

00:38:45.990 --> 00:38:47.900
FATHER AS ROLE MODEL

00:39:00.960 --> 00:39:02.340
The first snow!

00:39:06.380 --> 00:39:08.380
POCHI

00:39:15.140 --> 00:39:16.850
First snow! Let's take a picture!

00:39:17.850 --> 00:39:19.440
Why?

00:39:19.520 --> 00:39:21.060
How childish.

00:39:21.520 --> 00:39:23.110
Shut the door. It's cold.

00:39:50.590 --> 00:39:51.800
Where's the camera?

00:39:52.470 --> 00:39:55.220
In the top drawer, where else?

00:40:01.810 --> 00:40:02.770
It's gone!

00:40:07.480 --> 00:40:09.490
The camera's supposed to be here.

00:40:11.780 --> 00:40:13.700
This is the best part.

00:41:15.220 --> 00:41:18.300
<i>A lone figure, back turned,</i>
<i>receding into the mist.</i>

00:41:18.390 --> 00:41:19.850
<i>Santoka.</i>

00:41:24.270 --> 00:41:26.190
YAMADA FAMILY CHRONICLES

00:41:26.900 --> 00:41:28.310
YAMADA TAKASHI

00:41:30.020 --> 00:41:32.320
Happy New Year!

00:41:32.780 --> 00:41:33.990
<i>New Year's Cards.</i>

00:41:37.820 --> 00:41:38.780
Ready!

00:41:40.240 --> 00:41:41.580
-Go!
-Mine, mine,

00:41:41.660 --> 00:41:48.000
Mother's, Matsuko's, Nonoko's,

00:41:48.250 --> 00:41:53.880
Mother's, Matsuko's, Nonoko's,

00:41:53.960 --> 00:41:57.970
Mother's, Matsuko's, Nonoko's...

00:41:59.640 --> 00:42:01.810
Thirty-one seconds! A new record.

00:42:03.600 --> 00:42:04.640
Not bad.

00:42:08.980 --> 00:42:10.400
<i>The Thick of Winter.</i>

00:42:16.780 --> 00:42:18.030
Think I'll just...

00:42:18.110 --> 00:42:19.660
Get me some cake.

00:42:19.740 --> 00:42:20.700
Cola for me.

00:42:20.780 --> 00:42:21.660
And tangerines.

00:42:21.740 --> 00:42:23.830
The stove needs kerosene.

00:42:26.790 --> 00:42:29.210
Thank you!

00:42:40.430 --> 00:42:42.010
<i>Spring Showers.</i>

00:42:43.600 --> 00:42:45.640
Can you bring my umbrella?

00:42:45.720 --> 00:42:48.770
<i>Your father needs his umbrella.</i>

00:42:49.350 --> 00:42:52.360
<i>Why me? I'm studying.</i>

00:42:52.440 --> 00:42:55.860
<i>You should go.</i>
<i>Walk in the rain with your man.</i>

00:42:55.940 --> 00:42:59.530
<i>I don't have the energy.</i>

00:42:59.610 --> 00:43:02.830
<i>Noboru! You go, please.</i>

00:43:02.910 --> 00:43:04.080
<i>Make Nonoko go.</i>

00:43:04.370 --> 00:43:06.660
Forget it! I'll buy one.

00:43:06.750 --> 00:43:08.960
<i>Pick up some pork.</i>

00:43:09.290 --> 00:43:10.210
Idiots!

00:44:28.490 --> 00:44:32.410
<i>A spring shower, dressed for rain,</i>
<i>talking as they go.</i>

00:44:32.500 --> 00:44:33.580
<i>Buson.</i>

00:44:40.380 --> 00:44:43.800
Strange... Where's Noboru's sock?

00:44:43.880 --> 00:44:46.930
Nonoko's pajamas and Dad's towel?

00:44:47.810 --> 00:44:49.390
Pajamas? Socks?

00:44:49.470 --> 00:44:50.890
And his towel.

00:44:54.900 --> 00:44:56.400
Hey, wait...

00:44:58.230 --> 00:44:59.730
This means...

00:45:06.490 --> 00:45:08.700
I knew it!

00:45:08.780 --> 00:45:10.580
The Black Hole!

00:45:11.080 --> 00:45:13.000
THE PERFECT COMBO

00:45:14.540 --> 00:45:17.500
Maybe we'll order sushi in for dinner.

00:45:19.090 --> 00:45:23.380
Oh, what a waste of money!
I'll make the sushi.

00:45:24.050 --> 00:45:25.720
Just as I hoped.

00:45:30.430 --> 00:45:32.640
Say, Mother...

00:45:32.720 --> 00:45:36.350
Sushi's not interesting.
I thought I'd go gourmet.

00:45:39.110 --> 00:45:41.360
I see. So, what is it?

00:45:41.440 --> 00:45:44.320
Beef Stroganoga...

00:45:44.400 --> 00:45:46.570
Don't cook what you can't spell.

00:45:46.660 --> 00:45:47.780
Well, excuse me!

00:45:49.740 --> 00:45:52.700
It's Beef Stroganoff, right?

00:45:53.290 --> 00:45:54.790
You knew all along.

00:45:55.580 --> 00:45:56.830
I know very well.

00:45:57.420 --> 00:46:02.000
Beef Stroganoga is just
the Strogaffgaff of beef.

00:46:02.090 --> 00:46:04.300
Whatever, just make it.

00:46:05.880 --> 00:46:08.760
Darn. I was really counting on sushi.

00:46:24.190 --> 00:46:27.820
No good. I screwed it up. Order the sushi.

00:46:28.320 --> 00:46:30.240
BREAKFAST OF CHAMPIONS

00:46:34.120 --> 00:46:36.710
Wow, miso soup, fried egg, and seaweed.

00:46:38.120 --> 00:46:40.500
A real Japanese breakfast.

00:46:40.580 --> 00:46:42.500
Well, actually...

00:46:45.460 --> 00:46:46.510
Nonoko's leftovers?

00:46:48.800 --> 00:46:49.640
Yesterday's soup?

00:46:51.470 --> 00:46:52.550
Extra seaweed from lunch?

00:46:54.010 --> 00:46:55.430
Precisely!

00:46:56.890 --> 00:46:59.190
Today's your lucky day.

00:46:59.270 --> 00:47:00.310
Hardly!

00:47:03.190 --> 00:47:04.690
Take care.

00:47:07.150 --> 00:47:08.200
Matsuko.

00:47:17.660 --> 00:47:20.080
When's lunch, Matsuko?

00:47:22.290 --> 00:47:26.670
What are you talking about? We just ate.

00:47:27.420 --> 00:47:29.630
You're too young to be senile.

00:47:30.050 --> 00:47:31.390
Are you sure?

00:47:31.470 --> 00:47:35.140
The noodles, a few... Oops!

00:47:38.680 --> 00:47:40.770
I ate them all myself.

00:47:41.020 --> 00:47:42.230
Hey!

00:47:50.240 --> 00:47:51.990
-What's for dinner?
-Shabu shabu.

00:47:54.910 --> 00:47:57.290
We have it all the time.

00:47:57.370 --> 00:47:59.660
Shabu shabu's perfect for winter.

00:48:03.830 --> 00:48:05.710
OK, help yourselves.

00:48:06.710 --> 00:48:09.170
This way, she doesn't have to cook.

00:48:10.260 --> 00:48:12.840
Cold noodles for lunch again?

00:48:12.930 --> 00:48:14.720
That's what we had yesterday!

00:48:14.800 --> 00:48:17.140
And the day before.

00:48:17.220 --> 00:48:18.470
That doesn't make sense!

00:48:20.100 --> 00:48:22.100
And again tomorrow!?

00:48:22.520 --> 00:48:25.980
Noodles! What else?

00:48:26.980 --> 00:48:29.820
Lots of free ginger
in the garden to go with it.

00:48:31.070 --> 00:48:32.990
GINGER MORNING

00:48:35.740 --> 00:48:38.620
The ginger's good in miso soup.

00:48:38.700 --> 00:48:43.250
Yes, though they do say
it makes you forgetful.

00:48:44.250 --> 00:48:46.670
Oh, dear. He left his bag.

00:48:47.590 --> 00:48:50.510
He's bound to notice.
He can't be that dumb.

00:48:51.590 --> 00:48:53.590
-Right.
-Oh, no, I forgot...

00:49:03.690 --> 00:49:05.730
to take off my pajamas!

00:49:10.440 --> 00:49:11.360
I'm off.

00:49:11.440 --> 00:49:12.440
OK.

00:49:14.860 --> 00:49:16.320
Have a nice day.

00:49:21.040 --> 00:49:22.290
I'm off.

00:49:25.460 --> 00:49:26.420
My shoes!

00:49:31.130 --> 00:49:32.300
Mom, look!

00:49:33.800 --> 00:49:34.930
Dad!

00:49:35.220 --> 00:49:36.890
What's all the fuss?

00:49:37.640 --> 00:49:38.470
My train!

00:49:38.550 --> 00:49:39.640
I'll be late!

00:49:40.430 --> 00:49:41.810
Be careful.

00:49:45.600 --> 00:49:47.350
I'm off to school.

00:49:47.900 --> 00:49:49.820
Off you go.

00:49:52.570 --> 00:49:54.900
Can't even close the door behind them.

00:50:04.410 --> 00:50:05.540
What's this?

00:50:05.910 --> 00:50:08.710
Oh, Nonoko forgot her lunch.

00:50:08.790 --> 00:50:10.380
She needs it by noon?

00:50:10.460 --> 00:50:12.130
Sure, but...

00:50:13.000 --> 00:50:16.090
Fine, I'll take it to her
when I go shopping.

00:50:16.170 --> 00:50:18.470
That'll really be a help.

00:50:23.520 --> 00:50:24.850
I'm off.

00:50:24.930 --> 00:50:27.350
OK. Thank you.

00:50:33.020 --> 00:50:33.900
What's this?

00:50:37.110 --> 00:50:40.450
Oh, no, she's forgotten
her purse and everything.

00:50:44.200 --> 00:50:45.410
She'll be back.

00:50:50.500 --> 00:50:52.420
Watch the house, OK?

00:50:57.260 --> 00:50:59.930
Oh no! I left the kettle on.

00:51:02.510 --> 00:51:04.510
POCHI

00:51:04.890 --> 00:51:07.600
Mrs. Yamada, delivery!

00:51:09.850 --> 00:51:11.400
Are they out?

00:51:13.110 --> 00:51:16.150
No, they're in.

00:51:17.150 --> 00:51:18.570
Oh, Mrs. Yamada.

00:51:23.240 --> 00:51:25.620
Oh, I did turn it off.

00:51:26.540 --> 00:51:28.330
Were you robbed?

00:51:39.760 --> 00:51:40.760
Here's your package.

00:51:42.760 --> 00:51:44.390
Oh, thank you.

00:51:45.430 --> 00:51:46.350
Your seal?

00:51:46.430 --> 00:51:47.850
Oh, sorry.

00:51:48.310 --> 00:51:52.190
Let's see... Where do I keep it?

00:51:52.270 --> 00:51:55.860
It's in the back of the second drawer.

00:51:55.940 --> 00:51:57.780
Oh, goodness.

00:51:59.690 --> 00:52:01.240
Always a pleasure.

00:52:01.320 --> 00:52:02.570
Thank you.

00:52:05.950 --> 00:52:08.500
I delivered Nonoko's lunch.

00:52:08.910 --> 00:52:13.000
Why, Mother, I thought
you were going shopping.

00:52:13.580 --> 00:52:16.000
Oops, I forgot.

00:52:19.170 --> 00:52:21.680
Too much ginger!

00:52:23.220 --> 00:52:26.140
REGRET

00:52:40.740 --> 00:52:41.700
Say...

00:52:45.660 --> 00:52:47.280
Is that Mahler?

00:52:49.790 --> 00:52:54.040
I didn't know she was
a classical music fan.

00:53:13.020 --> 00:53:16.440
ART IS BRIEF LIFE IS LONG

00:53:22.280 --> 00:53:24.200
They're in full bloom.

00:53:28.830 --> 00:53:32.790
I wonder how many more times
I'll see the cherry blossoms.

00:53:33.910 --> 00:53:38.340
Don't be silly, Mother. You're only 70.

00:53:39.500 --> 00:53:41.840
Thirty more seasons?

00:53:54.430 --> 00:53:57.190
Mom, will you go pay the taxes?

00:53:57.270 --> 00:53:58.480
Leave it to me.

00:54:00.900 --> 00:54:03.070
You hand it to the clerk, got that?

00:54:03.150 --> 00:54:05.950
I know. Don't treat me like a child.

00:54:11.080 --> 00:54:15.000
Oh, dear, what a terrible calamity.

00:54:15.080 --> 00:54:16.160
POST OFFICE

00:54:16.250 --> 00:54:18.420
I'm really going senile.

00:54:19.580 --> 00:54:20.960
Nice to see you.

00:54:21.040 --> 00:54:23.340
Take care, bye.

00:54:27.720 --> 00:54:29.590
I put it in the mail box!

00:54:36.600 --> 00:54:41.060
Why, Shige.
Thanks for coming to visit.

00:54:41.440 --> 00:54:44.990
Well, I heard you were
suddenly hospitalized.

00:54:45.070 --> 00:54:47.900
You'll never believe it.

00:54:48.530 --> 00:54:50.280
Have a seat.

00:54:58.620 --> 00:54:59.710
You see...

00:54:59.790 --> 00:55:00.750
Yes.

00:55:02.290 --> 00:55:03.290
Look.

00:55:04.340 --> 00:55:07.340
See the guy visiting
that patient over there?

00:55:07.970 --> 00:55:11.470
I'm sure they're having an affair.

00:55:11.550 --> 00:55:12.850
What?

00:55:15.930 --> 00:55:17.390
Are you sure?

00:55:17.810 --> 00:55:22.400
They definitely look suspicious to me!

00:55:26.110 --> 00:55:27.820
Suspicious, right?

00:55:32.990 --> 00:55:34.740
This is a special room.

00:55:34.830 --> 00:55:39.160
That notorious city councilman
accused of corruption is in there now.

00:55:43.290 --> 00:55:47.210
I occasionally come up here
for a breath of fresh air.

00:55:54.510 --> 00:55:57.600
These noodles are pretty good, right?

00:55:58.560 --> 00:55:59.480
They are.

00:56:04.440 --> 00:56:08.900
But the coffee's really lousy here.

00:56:10.860 --> 00:56:14.820
By the way, why are you in the hospital?

00:56:22.080 --> 00:56:23.500
Oh, Shige!

00:56:29.840 --> 00:56:33.800
<i>No sign of death's approach</i>
<i>in the cicada's voices.</i>

00:56:33.890 --> 00:56:34.840
<i>Basho.</i>

00:56:40.930 --> 00:56:42.480
Why, Mother.

00:56:45.400 --> 00:56:46.480
Turn on the light.

00:56:47.690 --> 00:56:51.320
Oh, I hadn't noticed it getting dark.

00:57:02.710 --> 00:57:06.250
Noboru! Turn off your light.

00:57:06.330 --> 00:57:07.500
I'm not asleep!

00:57:09.670 --> 00:57:12.590
AGE COMES MORE EASILY THAN WISDOM

00:57:13.880 --> 00:57:17.640
Five problems left. I'm so sleepy.

00:57:19.930 --> 00:57:22.890
A hot bath will wake you up.

00:57:39.120 --> 00:57:40.080
In you go.

00:57:47.750 --> 00:57:50.800
-Feel better?
-Yup! I'm wide awake.

00:57:53.670 --> 00:57:57.050
OK, here goes!

00:57:58.010 --> 00:58:01.220
Here goes. Here goes.

00:58:02.390 --> 00:58:03.680
Here goes...

00:58:13.740 --> 00:58:17.660
He's as limp as a noodle.

00:58:19.160 --> 00:58:21.490
Don't give up.

00:58:21.580 --> 00:58:26.160
In a fire, the first five minutes count.
In a test, it's the last five minutes.

00:58:33.840 --> 00:58:37.510
Time's up. Turn in your papers.

00:58:37.590 --> 00:58:38.840
MIDTERM EXAM

00:58:41.800 --> 00:58:42.850
Ma'am!

00:58:43.520 --> 00:58:46.850
Tanaka went to
the nurse's office for ten minutes!

00:58:47.270 --> 00:58:48.100
Yes?

00:58:48.600 --> 00:58:50.480
That should be "lost time".

00:58:51.730 --> 00:58:52.690
I'm afraid not.

00:58:58.490 --> 00:59:00.950
Put them in the upstairs closet?

00:59:01.030 --> 00:59:01.870
Sure.

00:59:30.230 --> 00:59:32.610
Why's Noboru studying like a demon?

00:59:33.770 --> 00:59:37.150
His exams are over.

00:59:37.240 --> 00:59:38.860
He did miserably.

00:59:50.790 --> 00:59:53.630
About Noboru's tutor...

00:59:54.170 --> 00:59:55.380
He really needs one?

00:59:56.090 --> 00:59:57.800
He's my son, after all.

00:59:58.130 --> 00:59:59.170
You've got a point.

01:00:02.640 --> 01:00:06.350
But isn't it expensive?

01:00:06.890 --> 01:00:10.480
Three hundred dollars for two sessions
with a university student.

01:00:10.810 --> 01:00:12.100
What?

01:00:13.060 --> 01:00:15.360
For $300, I'll teach him.

01:00:15.440 --> 01:00:17.860
I'll teach him for $200.

01:00:19.610 --> 01:00:21.820
Pay me $100, and I'll work harder!

01:00:25.240 --> 01:00:28.330
This is getting us nowhere.

01:00:34.250 --> 01:00:37.550
<i>Fleeting dreams.</i>
<i>An octopus making its home in a trap,</i>

01:00:37.630 --> 01:00:39.460
<i>a summer moon.</i>

01:00:39.550 --> 01:00:41.590
<i>Basho.</i>

01:00:48.890 --> 01:00:50.020
I'm home!

01:00:50.100 --> 01:00:51.680
POCHI

01:00:57.150 --> 01:00:58.440
Look, chocolates!

01:01:01.150 --> 01:01:02.450
Mommy!

01:01:02.530 --> 01:01:06.240
Noboru bought chocolates!

01:01:06.320 --> 01:01:08.950
They were a Valentine's Day present!

01:01:09.990 --> 01:01:11.910
ADOLESCENCE

01:01:12.750 --> 01:01:13.750
Gone!

01:01:14.210 --> 01:01:15.920
Gone, gone, gone!

01:01:16.000 --> 01:01:17.170
I'm home!

01:01:18.380 --> 01:01:20.880
Where are those cookies, Nonoko?

01:01:20.960 --> 01:01:21.800
I ate them.

01:01:22.300 --> 01:01:25.430
What? I got them for a girl!

01:01:25.800 --> 01:01:26.970
But...

01:01:27.050 --> 01:01:28.260
No ifs, ands, or buts!

01:01:28.930 --> 01:01:31.520
Mommy already ate half.

01:01:31.970 --> 01:01:33.180
Mother?

01:01:44.030 --> 01:01:46.530
Damn... I forgot my umbrella.

01:01:47.120 --> 01:01:48.280
Hey, Yamada!

01:01:49.490 --> 01:01:50.790
Use my umbrella.

01:01:51.330 --> 01:01:52.620
How about you?

01:01:52.700 --> 01:01:53.830
I'll be fine.

01:01:55.790 --> 01:01:58.840
Say, Tanaka, I forgot my umbrella!

01:01:59.670 --> 01:02:01.880
Too bad. Don't catch a cold.

01:02:10.890 --> 01:02:12.220
Rejected.

01:02:14.100 --> 01:02:15.020
No!

01:02:17.060 --> 01:02:18.100
Give it back!

01:02:18.190 --> 01:02:19.360
Not after that.

01:02:19.440 --> 01:02:20.440
But it's mine.

01:02:20.520 --> 01:02:21.570
Thanks for the favor.

01:02:21.650 --> 01:02:23.320
-Give it back!
-I said no!

01:02:23.400 --> 01:02:24.820
Guess it's a rain date.

01:02:29.910 --> 01:02:31.620
Hey, Nakamura.

01:02:31.700 --> 01:02:33.240
Back to sock the teacher?

01:02:34.410 --> 01:02:37.250
Don't be stupid. I came to tell him
I got into college.

01:02:38.120 --> 01:02:39.790
Wow, you made it!

01:02:45.970 --> 01:02:47.050
Sir?

01:02:47.130 --> 01:02:48.010
No need to run

01:02:48.680 --> 01:02:49.840
from Nakamura.

01:02:49.930 --> 01:02:52.640
Idiot! Don't believe the rumors.

01:02:54.600 --> 01:02:56.140
Hey, Yamada, Yamashita,

01:02:57.100 --> 01:02:58.640
let's buy some dirty books.

01:03:00.730 --> 01:03:04.320
HITOMI

01:03:04.400 --> 01:03:07.780
DREAMING GIRL

01:03:07.860 --> 01:03:11.370
PHOTO BOOK

01:03:11.990 --> 01:03:12.830
Hey!

01:03:13.830 --> 01:03:14.700
Shoot!

01:03:16.700 --> 01:03:17.960
What a coincidence.

01:03:22.000 --> 01:03:26.090
<i>Tragedy in Bosnia!</i>
You've got serious taste.

01:03:26.170 --> 01:03:29.130
Well, Japan's part of a bigger world.

01:03:31.340 --> 01:03:33.300
Can I borrow it later?

01:03:36.140 --> 01:03:37.810
A real tragedy.

01:03:41.150 --> 01:03:42.310
I'm home.

01:03:44.900 --> 01:03:46.150
Noboru.

01:03:47.320 --> 01:03:48.740
The textbook?

01:03:48.820 --> 01:03:49.700
This?

01:03:50.150 --> 01:03:52.030
I gave you $10 for it.

01:03:52.570 --> 01:03:53.620
I want to see it.

01:04:12.050 --> 01:04:13.300
F1 FOR MIDDLE SCHOOL

01:04:13.390 --> 01:04:14.720
What is this?

01:04:16.180 --> 01:04:18.930
<i>Formula-1 Racing for Students</i>?

01:04:19.020 --> 01:04:22.060
It'll help my English and my geography.

01:04:24.230 --> 01:04:25.150
You idiot!

01:04:25.860 --> 01:04:27.690
You're the one who gave me

01:04:27.780 --> 01:04:31.070
<i>The Power Ranger's ABC</i> when I was three!

01:04:32.200 --> 01:04:35.450
Noboru, there's a girl on the phone.

01:04:35.530 --> 01:04:36.780
What?

01:04:43.460 --> 01:04:44.540
Oh, hello.

01:04:45.630 --> 01:04:46.790
Oh, yeah, it's me.

01:04:58.390 --> 01:04:59.930
Go away!

01:05:02.890 --> 01:05:05.310
Oh, no, nothing.

01:05:07.400 --> 01:05:10.780
Yeah, yeah, OK.

01:05:14.450 --> 01:05:16.490
A girlfriend... with his looks?

01:05:16.570 --> 01:05:17.830
A real girlfriend?

01:05:17.910 --> 01:05:19.040
His face is red.

01:05:19.830 --> 01:05:21.120
Yeah, OK.

01:05:21.750 --> 01:05:23.410
Bye, then.

01:05:35.720 --> 01:05:37.640
It's pounding away!

01:05:37.720 --> 01:05:38.890
An irregular heartbeat?

01:05:38.970 --> 01:05:40.010
Let's see.

01:05:51.440 --> 01:05:52.940
Do you think he's upset?

01:05:53.030 --> 01:05:55.860
You insulted him, Mother.

01:05:55.950 --> 01:05:59.030
This, from the paragon of motherhood?

01:06:43.040 --> 01:06:45.960
MARCH

01:06:48.290 --> 01:06:52.500
<i>The scent of plums on a mountain path.</i>
<i>Suddenly, dawn.</i>

01:06:52.590 --> 01:06:53.880
<i>Basho.</i>

01:06:53.960 --> 01:06:55.880
YAMADA FAMILY CHRONICLES

01:06:58.630 --> 01:07:00.010
I'm home.

01:07:00.090 --> 01:07:01.760
Welcome back.

01:07:04.180 --> 01:07:05.600
<i>An Autumn Night.</i>

01:07:12.730 --> 01:07:13.980
I'm hungry.

01:07:16.150 --> 01:07:17.150
Anything to eat?

01:07:17.990 --> 01:07:18.990
Coming right up.

01:07:26.870 --> 01:07:28.750
Red bean cake or banana.

01:07:32.210 --> 01:07:36.590
Who the hell would want
to come home to bean cakes

01:07:37.380 --> 01:07:39.470
after working hard all day?

01:07:41.260 --> 01:07:42.600
OK, a banana.

01:07:43.350 --> 01:07:46.970
What a jerk! Who wants a banana?

01:09:36.830 --> 01:09:41.170
<i>Turn towards me, I'm lonely too.</i>
<i>The Autumn dusk.</i>

01:09:41.340 --> 01:09:42.340
<i>Basho.</i>

01:09:45.680 --> 01:09:49.350
Mom's down with a cold.
We'll get take-out tonight.

01:09:49.430 --> 01:09:50.260
Seaweed-rice special.

01:09:50.350 --> 01:09:51.430
Me too!

01:09:51.520 --> 01:09:52.430
I'll have the salmon-rice.

01:09:53.560 --> 01:09:54.850
How about you, Mother?

01:09:55.390 --> 01:09:56.690
The combination special.

01:09:58.940 --> 01:09:59.940
I'll go get it!

01:10:00.270 --> 01:10:01.780
Not so fast!

01:10:05.780 --> 01:10:07.950
Tempura-rice for me!

01:10:08.030 --> 01:10:09.950
GOING MY WAY

01:10:10.030 --> 01:10:12.950
CROQUET TOURNAMENT

01:10:13.700 --> 01:10:15.160
That's good.

01:10:15.250 --> 01:10:17.420
GATEBALL COMPETITION

01:10:17.500 --> 01:10:19.420
Hey, hey, lady.

01:10:21.130 --> 01:10:22.460
You can't do that!

01:10:23.260 --> 01:10:25.470
What? But this is...

01:10:25.550 --> 01:10:26.550
GATEBALL COMPETITION
JULY 22ND

01:10:26.630 --> 01:10:30.640
It's empty now, but someone may
put a poster up. There's an election.

01:10:30.720 --> 01:10:32.890
But, mister...

01:10:34.180 --> 01:10:35.520
AWA YOICHIRO

01:10:35.600 --> 01:10:37.850
This was the only thing underneath.

01:10:45.690 --> 01:10:48.240
If it isn't old Saburo.

01:10:50.410 --> 01:10:52.990
This is my territory.

01:10:53.080 --> 01:10:55.620
Oh, it's you, Shige.

01:10:56.000 --> 01:10:58.710
We might as well work together,
we're volunteers.

01:11:04.510 --> 01:11:07.300
That's your side, this is mine.

01:11:08.880 --> 01:11:10.010
No trespassing.

01:11:10.720 --> 01:11:14.770
Amazing, she hasn't changed
a bit in 60 years.

01:11:17.520 --> 01:11:20.900
Oh, no, I forgot to take out the garbage.

01:11:23.940 --> 01:11:26.070
Oh, well, I'll have to sort it!

01:11:26.150 --> 01:11:29.410
Why sort burnables?

01:11:30.740 --> 01:11:32.740
Trash can at the station,

01:11:32.830 --> 01:11:35.740
Nonoko does the park,
Noboru does the store.

01:11:36.700 --> 01:11:37.830
You can't do that!

01:11:37.910 --> 01:11:40.170
Why not? It's a great plan.

01:11:40.710 --> 01:11:41.540
Off we go.

01:11:41.630 --> 01:11:43.040
See you later.

01:11:45.250 --> 01:11:46.130
Ouch!

01:11:46.210 --> 01:11:50.590
I volunteer to clean up the park,
and you dump trash there!

01:11:50.680 --> 01:11:53.680
I'm not dumping,
just using the public trash cans.

01:11:54.350 --> 01:11:55.810
That's the problem!

01:11:56.060 --> 01:11:57.980
Mom!

01:12:12.530 --> 01:12:14.450
THE FIGHT FOR JUSTICE

01:12:15.200 --> 01:12:16.490
Excuse us!

01:12:19.500 --> 01:12:21.120
Our ball fell in.

01:12:25.670 --> 01:12:30.220
This new one or this rubber ball?

01:12:32.510 --> 01:12:33.840
The rubber ball!

01:12:44.400 --> 01:12:47.570
Honesty's the best policy. Don't ever lie.

01:12:48.530 --> 01:12:49.530
OK.

01:12:50.240 --> 01:12:51.700
Take this one too.

01:12:53.030 --> 01:12:54.320
Wow! Thanks!

01:13:02.160 --> 01:13:05.460
Excuse me. Our ball fell in yesterday.

01:13:05.540 --> 01:13:06.960
But you weren't here.

01:13:07.040 --> 01:13:09.510
Didn't see any.

01:13:10.550 --> 01:13:11.800
I see...

01:13:13.130 --> 01:13:15.720
I'm sure this was the house.

01:13:21.060 --> 01:13:25.980
I beg you, please tell those boys
to give him his new ball back.

01:13:32.860 --> 01:13:35.030
Oh, poor things.

01:13:35.110 --> 01:13:38.910
You're right, they're all wilted.

01:13:39.580 --> 01:13:42.540
Not the flowers! The accident!

01:13:42.620 --> 01:13:43.750
Oh, I see.

01:13:44.830 --> 01:13:46.580
It was a motorcycle gang.

01:13:48.040 --> 01:13:51.000
The poor guard rail.

01:13:51.090 --> 01:13:51.920
Mother!

01:13:52.340 --> 01:13:56.430
It was the poor child's parents
who suffered.

01:14:30.170 --> 01:14:33.170
They're so loud,
it has to be a motorcycle gang.

01:14:33.590 --> 01:14:35.010
They're by the park.

01:14:35.630 --> 01:14:38.510
They're the litterbugs!

01:14:38.590 --> 01:14:39.970
I'll go scold them.

01:14:40.050 --> 01:14:41.890
That's dangerous, Mother!

01:14:41.970 --> 01:14:44.430
Someone was recently murdered for that.

01:14:44.520 --> 01:14:46.440
SENIOR CITIZEN MURDERED

01:14:47.140 --> 01:14:48.940
Hmm, I know.

01:14:57.990 --> 01:14:59.660
That's worse!

01:15:07.960 --> 01:15:10.750
M-mother! Why the get-up?

01:15:11.420 --> 01:15:14.090
She wants to scold the motorcycle gang.

01:15:14.170 --> 01:15:16.130
Won't you stop her, please?

01:15:17.800 --> 01:15:22.640
You can't wear that hard-hat. It's
a memento from when we built the house.

01:15:23.390 --> 01:15:26.140
Oh. Well, that's too bad.

01:15:26.640 --> 01:15:29.270
I'm sorry, but you can't.

01:15:29.980 --> 01:15:31.230
In that case...

01:15:31.310 --> 01:15:33.690
you wear it, and go.

01:15:33.770 --> 01:15:35.280
Me?

01:15:36.150 --> 01:15:40.530
They're not vicious.
They'll go home eventually.

01:15:40.990 --> 01:15:43.830
Then you have nothing to fear.

01:15:43.910 --> 01:15:47.160
Give them a manly scolding. You're older.

01:15:47.960 --> 01:15:48.790
Manly...?

01:15:49.080 --> 01:15:50.920
But, Mother...

01:15:51.000 --> 01:15:53.130
I know, let's report them to 911.

01:15:53.210 --> 01:15:57.550
The poor kids. They don't deserve
a criminal record for making noise.

01:15:58.220 --> 01:15:59.340
A record!

01:16:16.230 --> 01:16:17.780
See, they're gone.

01:16:18.900 --> 01:16:20.240
You think?

01:16:30.500 --> 01:16:31.580
What did I tell you?

01:16:34.880 --> 01:16:36.710
We're relying on you.

01:16:40.470 --> 01:16:42.680
All right, I'll just go look.

01:16:45.220 --> 01:16:47.560
Be careful, dear!

01:17:35.650 --> 01:17:37.730
Uhm, excuse me.

01:17:38.190 --> 01:17:39.650
What do you want?

01:17:39.730 --> 01:17:42.440
It's awfully late.

01:17:42.780 --> 01:17:43.860
Yeah? So what?

01:17:47.370 --> 01:17:49.080
Got a problem?

01:17:49.160 --> 01:17:52.870
No, we can work this out.
I don't have a problem.

01:17:53.210 --> 01:17:55.920
I don't have a problem,

01:17:56.000 --> 01:17:59.250
-but I do have a request.
-Spit it out.

01:18:01.420 --> 01:18:02.880
Ask away, old man.

01:18:04.010 --> 01:18:06.510
Would you mind turning off your headlight?

01:18:07.180 --> 01:18:09.510
So that's your request, then?

01:18:10.850 --> 01:18:11.850
Uhm, no.

01:18:11.930 --> 01:18:13.270
What do you want then?

01:18:18.610 --> 01:18:24.320
<i>Come, come fireflies</i>
<i>This water's bitter, this water's sweet</i>

01:18:24.400 --> 01:18:25.490
What is that?

01:18:29.450 --> 01:18:32.580
<i>That water's sweet</i>

01:18:34.750 --> 01:18:36.420
<i>Come, fireflies</i>

01:18:37.420 --> 01:18:38.880
That old bag's nuts.

01:18:39.460 --> 01:18:41.170
Mother, are you all right?

01:18:44.920 --> 01:18:46.260
An old bag, huh?

01:18:46.800 --> 01:18:50.930
At least turn down that putt-putt.
You're a neighborhood nuisance.

01:18:51.010 --> 01:18:53.470
Mother, you can't talk to these low-lifes.

01:18:53.560 --> 01:18:55.430
Who you calling low-life?

01:18:55.520 --> 01:18:57.980
How exciting!

01:18:58.060 --> 01:19:00.730
What a great voice you have.

01:19:00.810 --> 01:19:01.940
Mother!

01:19:02.400 --> 01:19:06.150
And a fine face and physique
to go with it.

01:19:06.240 --> 01:19:09.280
I bet people shut up when you talk.

01:19:09.610 --> 01:19:10.450
Get to the point!

01:19:11.320 --> 01:19:15.540
Oh, scary. You sure
shut this guy up in a hurry.

01:19:15.620 --> 01:19:16.540
Tell me about it.

01:19:16.620 --> 01:19:21.840
When you yell at people, it reminds me
of a snake staring down a frog.

01:19:23.960 --> 01:19:29.590
It sure must be fun shutting people up
and ordering them around.

01:19:29.970 --> 01:19:30.800
It's OK.

01:19:30.890 --> 01:19:36.220
I know, why don't you employ
your venom in the cause of justice?

01:19:37.020 --> 01:19:38.310
What?

01:19:38.390 --> 01:19:41.980
Don't you like fighting for justice,
that Masked Rider stuff?

01:19:44.020 --> 01:19:45.480
Way old, Granny.

01:19:45.570 --> 01:19:49.860
Of course, it's not exactly cool,
is it? Nowadays

01:19:49.950 --> 01:19:53.580
we turn a blind eye
to every kind of misdeed.

01:19:53.660 --> 01:19:57.330
But I know you could do it
because you're fearless.

01:19:59.160 --> 01:20:03.340
Someone tosses a cigarette butt
or can from their car,

01:20:03.420 --> 01:20:06.960
you use that voice of yours,
make them pick it up.

01:20:08.220 --> 01:20:11.720
You see a kid causing trouble
on the subway,

01:20:11.800 --> 01:20:14.640
you gently tap him on the shoulder.

01:20:15.260 --> 01:20:18.850
I'm sure anyone will do whatever you say.

01:20:18.930 --> 01:20:23.730
We'll all be so happy,
we'll cheer you on.

01:20:26.820 --> 01:20:30.650
It's nice to be appreciated.

01:20:31.200 --> 01:20:33.740
While you're at it, scare off thugs,

01:20:33.820 --> 01:20:37.540
and take the bad guys' money.

01:20:39.160 --> 01:20:44.080
What do you say, will you heed
an old bag's plea and fight for justice?

01:20:44.170 --> 01:20:48.630
It'll be a whole lot better
than listening to me rant and rave.

01:20:51.090 --> 01:20:53.390
I think this old lady's nuts.

01:20:54.640 --> 01:20:56.560
No go?

01:20:56.640 --> 01:21:01.060
What a shame, with your godly attributes.

01:21:04.310 --> 01:21:05.150
Let's go.

01:21:12.860 --> 01:21:15.450
Think about fighting for justice!

01:21:21.370 --> 01:21:22.410
Hey, you forgot this.

01:21:34.760 --> 01:21:35.930
Did he get it?

01:21:36.180 --> 01:21:37.930
Mother!

01:21:51.740 --> 01:21:55.610
Noboru! Nonoko!

01:21:55.700 --> 01:21:57.370
Mother!

01:22:51.290 --> 01:22:53.920
It's the Masked Rider!

01:22:57.010 --> 01:23:01.850
SCHOOL ZONE

01:23:34.590 --> 01:23:36.210
The Masked Rider!

01:24:20.260 --> 01:24:22.640
Help!

01:24:32.150 --> 01:24:33.270
Mother!

01:24:34.230 --> 01:24:35.570
Noboru!

01:24:37.190 --> 01:24:38.650
Nonoko!

01:24:52.040 --> 01:24:55.340
Thank you, Masked Rider!

01:25:43.380 --> 01:25:47.720
<i>How cruel: a grasshopper trapped</i>
<i>under a warrior's helmet.</i>

01:25:56.900 --> 01:25:58.110
I'm home.

01:25:58.190 --> 01:26:00.190
Did you bring your umbrella home?

01:26:01.360 --> 01:26:05.240
Your husband's home
from work, exhausted,

01:26:05.320 --> 01:26:09.580
and all you can ask is, "Did you
bring your umbrella home?"

01:26:09.660 --> 01:26:12.410
OK, OK. Welcome home. Have a hard day?

01:26:13.000 --> 01:26:14.210
Where's your umbrella?

01:26:15.370 --> 01:26:16.460
I forgot it.

01:26:16.540 --> 01:26:21.460
POCHI

01:26:22.510 --> 01:26:23.760
Welcome home.

01:26:23.840 --> 01:26:28.340
Look, I remembered
to bring it home, so there, ha!

01:26:32.680 --> 01:26:35.310
What? Got a problem?

01:26:36.940 --> 01:26:40.360
But you didn't take an umbrella today.

01:26:42.780 --> 01:26:43.610
See?

01:26:44.570 --> 01:26:46.490
SECTION CHIEF YAMADA

01:26:47.030 --> 01:26:48.320
I bought a cake.

01:26:48.410 --> 01:26:49.280
Really?

01:26:50.910 --> 01:26:53.160
Once in a blue moon.

01:26:54.160 --> 01:26:56.580
Guilty conscience?

01:26:56.660 --> 01:26:57.500
What was that?

01:26:57.580 --> 01:27:01.750
That's going too far.
Here, Takashi's thoughtfully gone and

01:27:01.840 --> 01:27:03.170
and I even bought custard.

01:27:05.720 --> 01:27:07.220
Now that's suspicious.

01:27:11.220 --> 01:27:16.390
Nonoko! Noboru! Your father got cake!

01:27:23.570 --> 01:27:24.980
Where's Dad?

01:27:25.070 --> 01:27:26.740
On a business trip.

01:27:27.610 --> 01:27:28.860
But his briefcase...

01:27:30.450 --> 01:27:33.450
Oh no, he must've forgotten it.

01:27:33.530 --> 01:27:34.910
And his scarf and train pass.

01:27:36.910 --> 01:27:37.870
What? Oh no!

01:27:38.500 --> 01:27:41.380
He was supposed to leave early.

01:27:41.580 --> 01:27:43.090
Father!

01:27:44.460 --> 01:27:45.710
Dear!

01:27:51.720 --> 01:27:52.640
SECTION CHIEF YAMADA

01:27:53.430 --> 01:27:54.930
Mom must've overslept.

01:27:56.350 --> 01:28:00.440
She woke up late
and thought Dad had already left.

01:28:00.520 --> 01:28:01.900
Oh, I see.

01:28:02.110 --> 01:28:05.230
I need this too.

01:28:09.700 --> 01:28:11.950
B-b-briefcase!

01:28:12.410 --> 01:28:14.030
H-h-here!

01:28:14.740 --> 01:28:15.660
I'm off!

01:28:16.040 --> 01:28:17.660
Have a nice trip!

01:28:21.830 --> 01:28:23.670
Be careful!

01:28:27.960 --> 01:28:29.260
I can still make it.

01:28:47.280 --> 01:28:50.190
GOTO LIQUOR SHOP

01:28:57.330 --> 01:28:58.750
Are you OK?

01:29:11.220 --> 01:29:12.300
Phone, phone.

01:29:23.350 --> 01:29:25.560
I suddenly feel terrible.

01:29:29.320 --> 01:29:31.240
I can hardly breathe.

01:29:31.820 --> 01:29:34.860
Yes, yes, I'll get there.

01:29:35.620 --> 01:29:37.410
I'll crawl there if I have to.

01:29:38.330 --> 01:29:39.740
Please tell the client...

01:29:40.240 --> 01:29:43.500
Yes, yes, I'm terribly sorry.

01:29:48.710 --> 01:29:50.000
A slight fever.

01:29:51.300 --> 01:29:52.420
You should stay home.

01:29:53.840 --> 01:29:55.890
Before it gets worse.

01:29:55.970 --> 01:29:58.640
The company won't take care of you.

01:30:00.850 --> 01:30:04.310
You know, maybe I will.
Make a long weekend of it.

01:30:04.390 --> 01:30:06.600
You should, you should.

01:30:06.690 --> 01:30:09.940
It's good to relax
and enjoy some time at home.

01:30:26.580 --> 01:30:28.420
What is it?

01:30:30.750 --> 01:30:34.220
I started feeling better
the minute I decided to stay home.

01:30:34.970 --> 01:30:37.090
I guess I'll go in after all.

01:30:51.610 --> 01:30:53.030
Take care, dear.

01:32:01.050 --> 01:32:04.260
Next, Mr. Yamada
will offer his congratulations.

01:32:05.100 --> 01:32:07.270
Your notes, dear.

01:32:13.860 --> 01:32:15.780
He's wound tight as a spring!

01:32:23.740 --> 01:32:28.790
Uhm... This is a fine, auspicious day...

01:32:33.250 --> 01:32:36.670
CUCUMBER, GARBAGE BAGS, LIGHT BULBS

01:32:50.310 --> 01:32:52.730
Life is full of surprises...

01:32:58.570 --> 01:33:01.030
Now... that is, up until now...

01:33:02.070 --> 01:33:04.660
things seemed to be just fine...

01:33:06.280 --> 01:33:09.120
then suddenly,
you're shoved off a cliff...

01:33:09.580 --> 01:33:12.460
By... your trusted spouse...

01:33:12.870 --> 01:33:15.630
of all people!

01:33:16.920 --> 01:33:18.130
He means you.

01:33:20.260 --> 01:33:23.260
But Ichiro and Kazuko,

01:33:23.930 --> 01:33:27.970
you have to accept life as it comes.

01:33:30.890 --> 01:33:34.440
Acceptance is the key to surviving

01:33:34.520 --> 01:33:39.900
the worst situations
without losing heart or breaking up.

01:33:40.610 --> 01:33:42.610
Breaking up?

01:33:44.490 --> 01:33:46.280
Even the worst behavior

01:33:47.070 --> 01:33:52.040
can be accepted and forgiven
if there is no malice.

01:33:52.120 --> 01:33:54.920
In fact, it must be forgiven
so one can go on with life!

01:33:55.620 --> 01:33:57.420
Gutsy speech!

01:33:58.090 --> 01:34:03.130
It's not necessarily bad
to resign yourself to a situation.

01:34:03.630 --> 01:34:05.930
In fact, it's essential.

01:34:06.260 --> 01:34:09.060
A must for a happy family.

01:34:09.140 --> 01:34:12.060
A must for facing life
and getting on with it.

01:34:14.230 --> 01:34:17.440
Though it may sound negative,

01:34:18.310 --> 01:34:21.230
"acceptance"

01:34:21.650 --> 01:34:26.070
is the only way out of totally
unacceptable situations.

01:34:29.330 --> 01:34:33.750
I didn't know he had it in him.
What a man.

01:34:41.710 --> 01:34:45.420
Um, well, that is, I mean...

01:34:49.510 --> 01:34:52.350
So, my dear Ichiro and Kazuko,

01:34:53.020 --> 01:34:55.680
congratulations on your wedding.

01:34:57.440 --> 01:35:03.030
May you be a tough, harmonious couple.

01:35:13.950 --> 01:35:18.250
<i>When I grew up and fell in love</i>

01:35:18.330 --> 01:35:22.130
<i>I asked my sweetheart, what lies ahead?</i>

01:35:23.420 --> 01:35:30.220
<i>Will we have rainbows day after day?</i>
<i>Here's what my sweetheart said</i>

01:35:31.050 --> 01:35:34.220
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:35:34.310 --> 01:35:37.480
<i>Whatever will be, will be</i>

01:35:38.520 --> 01:35:42.060
<i>The future's not ours to see</i>

01:35:42.150 --> 01:35:44.940
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:35:46.360 --> 01:35:48.900
<i>What will be, will be</i>

01:35:50.990 --> 01:35:54.660
A skinhead cut
would disguise your baldness.

01:35:56.040 --> 01:35:57.080
Who asked you?

01:35:57.870 --> 01:36:00.880
-Don't you need dentures, Mother?
-Who asked you?

01:36:00.960 --> 01:36:03.380
Cut it out! Both of you!

01:36:03.460 --> 01:36:06.880
You're starting to look like
a sumo wrestler.

01:36:06.960 --> 01:36:08.630
-You tell her!
-How dare you?

01:36:11.430 --> 01:36:15.510
You're setting a terrible example
in front of the children.

01:36:15.600 --> 01:36:18.100
I can't hear the TV!

01:36:21.940 --> 01:36:24.150
I know why we're so peaceful.

01:36:25.820 --> 01:36:28.530
Because all three of you are nuts.

01:36:29.110 --> 01:36:31.160
-How dare you?
-How dare you?

01:36:32.280 --> 01:36:34.990
If even one of you were normal,

01:36:35.660 --> 01:36:37.580
it'd throw off the balance.

01:36:37.660 --> 01:36:41.080
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:36:41.170 --> 01:36:44.380
<i>Whatever will be, will be</i>

01:36:45.340 --> 01:36:49.050
<i>The future's not ours to see</i>

01:36:49.130 --> 01:36:51.930
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:36:53.220 --> 01:36:55.140
<i>What will be, will be</i>

01:36:55.220 --> 01:36:56.180
THIS YEAR'S RESOLUTION
MAKE FRIENDS, STUDY, HEALTH

01:36:56.260 --> 01:36:58.310
What's your motto?

01:36:58.390 --> 01:36:59.560
Getting married?

01:36:59.640 --> 01:37:00.640
A new job?

01:37:02.560 --> 01:37:04.100
Be quiet.

01:37:10.690 --> 01:37:11.860
This.

01:37:14.110 --> 01:37:17.830
"Don't overdo it."

01:37:17.910 --> 01:37:21.290
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:37:21.370 --> 01:37:25.380
<i>Whatever will be, will be</i>

01:37:25.460 --> 01:37:29.130
<i>The future's not ours to see</i>

01:37:29.210 --> 01:37:32.050
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:37:33.300 --> 01:37:36.260
<i>What will be, will be</i>

01:37:38.260 --> 01:37:42.180
<i>Now I have children of my own</i>

01:37:42.270 --> 01:37:46.270
<i>They ask their mother what will I be</i>

01:37:47.310 --> 01:37:51.280
<i>Will I be handsome? Will I be rich?</i>

01:37:51.360 --> 01:37:55.030
<i>I tell them tenderly</i>

01:37:55.110 --> 01:37:58.240
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:37:58.330 --> 01:38:01.750
<i>Whatever will be, will be</i>

01:38:02.500 --> 01:38:05.790
<i>The future's not ours to see</i>

01:38:06.210 --> 01:38:09.130
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:38:10.340 --> 01:38:13.170
<i>What will be, will be</i>

01:38:14.430 --> 01:38:18.100
<i>Que sera, sera</i>

01:38:31.690 --> 01:38:34.280
Hey, everybody's in the picture!

01:38:34.360 --> 01:38:35.650
Let's see.

01:38:35.740 --> 01:38:36.990
Everyone's so tiny.

01:38:37.070 --> 01:38:38.160
It's a stick-on picture.

01:38:41.450 --> 01:38:43.580
Time to get some dinner.

01:38:43.660 --> 01:38:44.710
Let's have pork cutlets.

01:38:44.790 --> 01:38:45.830
I want pizza!

01:38:45.910 --> 01:38:47.420
-Tempura.
-Spaghetti!

01:38:47.500 --> 01:38:49.040
Quiet! I decide!

01:39:19.110 --> 01:39:24.120
THE OCEAN IN SPRING THE GENTLE ROLLING
OF THE WAVES ALL DAY LONG.

01:39:24.200 --> 01:39:25.660
BUSON.
